 'check:endpoint-mobile-hardening':'The stated corporate ownership and permitted personal use distinguish COPE from personal BYOD and business-only COBO. This is an ungraded model-response reveal.',
 'section:endpoint-mobile-hardening:0':'Maintained configuration layers combine least privilege, supported-software patching, filtering/encryption, execution controls, credentials, telemetry and recovery. Prevention differs from EDR response and vendor-dependent XDR correlation.',
 'section:endpoint-mobile-hardening:1':'BYOD is user-owned; COPE/COBO are organization-owned with differing permitted use. CYOD selects from an approved list and explicitly allows either ownership depending on the programme.',
 'section:endpoint-mobile-hardening:2':'MDM/UEM capabilities depend on enrollment, platform, connectivity and legal policy. Radio proximity supplies no authentication/encryption guarantee; modified-device access requires an explicit policy decision.',
 'lesson:platform-cloud-hardening':'Partial navigation container for boot trust, constrained systems, cloud vocabulary and corroborated configuration/process signals. Its held cloud-table section is not approved by this parent disposition.',
 'keywords:platform-cloud-hardening':'Three bounded definitions distinguish reducing exposed features/settings, an approved maintained baseline and limited identity access/duration.',
 'traps:platform-cloud-hardening':'Cloud labels differ, an authorized boot chain does not prove an invulnerable OS, and a suspicious service-host relationship needs investigation rather than a conclusive injection verdict.',
 'check:platform-cloud-hardening':'Independent providers without portability binding support the multi-cloud description; the model response explicitly requires technology enabling data/application portability for hybrid and permits overlap when both conditions hold. Ungraded reveal only.',
 'section:platform-cloud-hardening:0':'UEFI boot signatures are one trust layer, with firmware/key/measured-boot/OS/physical controls still needed. RTOS predictable timing differs from general speed; embedded constraints and legitimate sideloading require provenance decisions.',
